                                                "sense_id": "10ddb706-2931-3452-8b6c-2545bab72f87",
                                                "text": "Carver's work, considered as a totality, constitutes what Bakhtin calls a chronotope, “a formally constitutive category of literature...[within which] spatial and temporal indicators are fused into one carefully thought—out, concrete whole."
                                            }
                                        ]
